     drawing's x-y plane and is extruded toward the viewer's lower left (30 degree axes, the points
     projected ahead of time so strokes keep their width): the back face, the edges joining it to
     the front, then the front face filled with the background so it hides what is behind it, a dot
     grid on it in the same projection. The ink is the white pushed a third of the way to the
     palette's accent (lilac-white on Colibri), soaked in: its edge bleeds a little and wavers, and
     its alpha thins unevenly, as ink in board. Callouts in the terminal's red slot (ansi1: apricot
     on Colibri) point at the parts on dashed leader lines, each disc marked with a sigil.
     Rasterized to .config/fastfetch/logo.png by fastfetch/render.sh.

     Drawn on the logo's 34x21 terminal cells at 10x22.5 units a cell (the terminal fits the picture
     to the cells); the summary runs from row 1 to 19, so the drawing stays inside y 22.5 to 450. -->
